# The build context is what the two Dockerfiles copy and nothing else: everything is left out, then each path they
# name is let back in. A household's config, data, store and secrets, the git history and development-only material
# never enter a build.
*
!.dockerignore
!.env.example
!.gitattributes
!.gitignore
!AGENTS.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!CLAUDE.md
!LICENSE
!Makefile
!NOTICE
!README.md
!THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES
!THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
!compose.yaml
!ff
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!app
!deploy
!etl
!examples
!starter
!tests
!tools
# the workflows, Dependabot's settings and the issue forms are tested inside the image
!.github
# the documents are tested inside the image: their links, the key reference against the validators' registry, the
# table of supported banks against the formats, the importers' example preset, the README's pictures
!CLA.md
!CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
!CONTRIBUTING.md
!SECURITY.md
!TRADEMARKS.md
!docs
# Inside what is let back in, what never ships: development-only material, installed and built files, caches,
# environment files (the example aside).
docs/dev
tools/private
app/node_modules
app/dist
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.DS_Store
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
